  "steps": [
    "Loaded the UCI Adult census data (48,842 people, 24% earn >50K) from OpenML.",
    "Renamed columns to simple names, marked missing answers as \u201cUnknown\u201d, dropped the census sampling weight.",
    "Built one scikit-learn Pipeline per model (one-hot encoding for categories, scaling for the linear model).",
    "Compared Logistic Regression, Random Forest, Gradient Boosting, XGBoost, LightGBM and CatBoost with 5-fold stratified cross-validation (ROC-AUC, F1, training time).",
    "Shipped XGBoost (best exportable model) and evaluated it once on a held-out 20% test set.",
    "Explained it with SHAP values and exported the whole pipeline to ONNX for the browser."
  ],
